1. The Software

"The Software" means TeselaDB in object code: the teseladb binary, the Docker
images that contain it, the install script, and their documentation, in every
version the Licensor publishes. The Software is distributed only in object code.
This license gives no right to its source code.

2. Use without production

You may install and run the Software, at no cost, to develop, test, evaluate,
study and demonstrate it, and in continuous integration, provided that it holds
no data of a production system.

3. Free production use, including commercial use

You may run the Software in production, at no cost and for any purpose,
including commercial purposes, when You do not offer it to third parties as a
hosted or managed service (section 5) and at least one of these conditions holds:

  (a) the nodes of the Software that Your organization runs in production at the
      same time, in every cluster, use 32 GB of RAM or less in total, whatever the
      revenue of Your organization; or

  (b) the total revenue of Your organization in its last completed fiscal year was
      less than EUR 1,000,000 (one million euros) or its equivalent in other
      currencies, whatever the RAM of its nodes; or

  (c) Your use is non-commercial: personal use, education, academic research, or
      use by a non-profit organization or a public administration, in each case
      not for the commercial benefit of a third party.

"Your organization" includes every entity that controls, is controlled by, or is
under common control with You.

The RAM of a node is the memory available to its process: the limit of its
container or control group (cgroup) when there is one, or the total memory of the
machine otherwise, rounded up to the whole gigabyte. The total is the sum of the
RAM of the nodes.

4. Commercial license

A separate commercial license from the Licensor is required for any production
use when none of the conditions of section 3 holds, that is, when the nodes of
Your organization use more than 32 GB of RAM in total, its revenue was
EUR 1,000,000 or more and the use is commercial. It is also required for the uses
of sections 5 and 6(e). See COMMERCIAL.md or https://teseladb.com/pricing.

5. Hosted or managed services

Offering the Software as a hosted or managed service means making its
functionality available to third parties who do not run it themselves, such as
selling a database service, a database platform or a managed cluster built on the
Software. It is not allowed under sections 2 and 3, whatever the size of Your
organization, and needs a commercial license that grants it expressly. Running the
Software as the database of Your own applications, even when Your customers use
those applications, is not a hosted or managed service.

